<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.6</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>UNAUDITED PRO FORMA CONDENSED COMBINED FINANCIAL
INFORMATION</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in"><I>Defined terms included below shall have the
same meaning as terms defined and included elsewhere in the Combined Company&rsquo;s (as defined below) Current Report on Form&nbsp;8-K
filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (the &ldquo;SEC&rdquo;) on August&nbsp;13, 2026 (the &ldquo;Form&nbsp;8-K&rdquo;).</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">On December&nbsp;17, 2025, Yarrow Bioscience,&nbsp;Inc.,
a Delaware corporation (&ldquo;Yarrow&rdquo;), entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger and Reorganization with VYNE Therapeutics
Inc., a Delaware corporation (&ldquo;VYNE&rdquo;), which was amended on January&nbsp;30, 2026 (as amended, the &ldquo;Merger Agreement&rdquo;),
pursuant to which, among other matters, Yellow Merger Sub Corp., a direct, wholly owned subsidiary of VYNE (&ldquo;Merger Sub&rdquo;),
merged with and into Yarrow, with Yarrow surviving as a wholly owned subsidiary of VYNE and the surviving corporation of the merger (the
&ldquo;Merger&rdquo;). Concurrently with the execution of the Merger Agreement, and in order to provide Yarrow with additional capital
for its development programs prior to the closing of the Merger (the &ldquo;Closing&rdquo;), certain existing investors entered into a
Securities Purchase Agreement (the &ldquo;Securities Purchase Agreement&rdquo;) with Yarrow, pursuant to which such investors purchased,
immediately prior to the Merger, shares of Yarrow&rsquo;s common stock (&ldquo;Yarrow Common Stock&rdquo;) or, in lieu thereof, pre-funded
warrants to purchase shares of Yarrow Common Stock (&ldquo;Yarrow Pre-Funded Warrants&rdquo;), for gross proceeds of approximately $100.0&nbsp;million
(the &ldquo;Yarrow Pre-Closing Financing&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">On July&nbsp;27, 2026 (the
&ldquo;Closing Date&rdquo;), Yarrow and VYNE completed the Merger in accordance with the terms of the Merger Agreement. In connection
with the completion of the Merger, Yarrow changed its name from &ldquo;Yarrow Bioscience,&nbsp;Inc.&rdquo; to &ldquo;Yarrow Bioscience Operating Company Corp.,&rdquo; VYNE changed its name to &ldquo;Yarrow Bioscience,&nbsp;Inc.&rdquo; and the current business of Yarrow
became the primary business of the Combined Company. VYNE following the Merger is referred to herein as the &ldquo;Combined Company.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">On the Closing Date, VYNE issued an aggregate
of 2,130,731 shares of VYNE&rsquo;s common stock (&ldquo;VYNE Common Stock&rdquo;) to Yarrow stockholders (after giving effect to the
1-for-50 reverse stock split of VYNE Common Stock in connection with the Merger), based on the exchange ratio of 0.7171 shares of VYNE
Common Stock for each share of Yarrow Common Stock (the &ldquo;Exchange Ratio&rdquo;), including those shares of Yarrow Common Stock issued
upon the conversion of Yarrow&rsquo;s Series&nbsp;A preferred stock (&ldquo;Yarrow Preferred Stock&rdquo;) and those shares of Yarrow
Common Stock issued in the Yarrow Pre-Closing Financing. In addition, the outstanding and unexercised Yarrow Pre-Funded Warrants and certain
shares of Yarrow Common Stock (including shares issued upon the conversion of Yarrow Preferred Stock and shares issued in the Yarrow Pre-Closing
Financing) were converted into 25,590,346 pre-funded warrants to purchase shares of VYNE Common Stock (&ldquo;VYNE Pre-Funded Warrants&rdquo;)
on the existing terms and conditions and outstanding options to purchase shares of Yarrow Common Stock (&ldquo;Yarrow Options&rdquo;)
were converted into 2,002,282 options to purchase shares of VYNE Common Stock (&ldquo;VYNE Options&rdquo;) on the existing terms and conditions
(including with respect to vesting and accelerated vesting).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The following unaudited pro&nbsp;forma condensed
combined financial information gives effect to the Merger, which, together with the Yarrow Pre-Closing Financing, has been accounted for
as a reverse recapitalization under generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America (&ldquo;U.S. GAAP&rdquo;).
For further details related to the accounting for the Merger, please see Notes 1 and 3 below. All share amounts have been adjusted to
reflect the Exchange Ratio, unless otherwise stated.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The unaudited pro&nbsp;forma condensed combined
balance sheet combines the historical balance sheets of VYNE and Yarrow as of June&nbsp;30, 2026 and depicts the accounting of the transactions
prepared pursuant to Article&nbsp;11 of Regulation&nbsp;S-X (the &ldquo;pro&nbsp;forma balance sheet transaction accounting adjustments&rdquo;).
The unaudited pro&nbsp;forma condensed combined statements of operations for the six months ended June&nbsp;30, 2026 for VYNE and Yarrow
and the unaudited pro&nbsp;forma condensed combined statements of operations for the year ended December&nbsp;31, 2025 for VYNE and the
period from October&nbsp;3, 2025 (inception) to December&nbsp;31, 2025 for Yarrow combine the historical results of VYNE and Yarrow for
those periods and depict the pro&nbsp;forma transaction accounting adjustments assuming that those adjustments were made as of January&nbsp;1,
2025 (the &ldquo;pro&nbsp;forma statements of operations transaction accounting adjustments&rdquo;). Collectively, the pro&nbsp;forma
balance sheet transaction accounting adjustments and the pro&nbsp;forma statements of operations transaction accounting adjustments are
referred to as the &ldquo;transaction accounting adjustments&rdquo; or &ldquo;pro&nbsp;forma adjustments.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

